• @predictor.What-If Thought: ## Summary of Research

  **Round 1** (all 16 teams, `get_team_seasonal_stats`, 2024–2025): Built an offense/defense EPA-based strength read. Offensive standouts in 2025 (passing_epa): LA (150.5), GB (118.8), DAL (115.0), SF (107.0), DET (103.4), SEA (68.3), CHI (47.9), PHI (31.9). Defensive standouts (sacks+INTs): ATL (73), SEA (65), LA (63), DET (61), MIN (57), CHI (58), PHI (54), NO (54), WAS (50).

  **Round 2** (deep dive, tool-confirmed): `get_transactions(PHI)` confirmed the actual trade: *"Traded WR A.J. Brown to New England for a 2028 first-round pick and a conditional 2027 fifth-round pick"* (2026-06-02), plus PHI separately acquired WR Dontayvion Wicks from GB. Current PHI roster (`get_current_roster`, WR) confirms A.J. Brown is absent; current WR corps is DeVonta Smith, Wicks, Elijah Moore, Marquise Brown, rookie Makai Lemon. `get_transactions(LA)` confirmed a major trade: Rams sent LB Jared Verse + 2027 1st/2028 2nd/2029 3rd to Cleveland for DE Myles Garrett, plus HC Sean McVay and GM Les Snead signed extensions. `get_transactions(GB)` confirmed DC hire of Jonathan Gannon, LaFleur/Gutekunst extensions, and LB Micah Parsons + TE Tucker Kraft + DT Javon Hargrave on the PUP list. `get_transactions(DET)` confirmed DBs Brian Branch and Kerby Joseph on the PUP list. `get_transactions(SF)` confirmed WR Ricky Pearsall placed on season-ending IR, with SF responding by adding Deebo Samuel, Christian Kirk, and Mike Evans. All `get_injury_report`/`get_coaching_changes`/`get_management_changes` calls returned "no data source available" for every team checked, so injury/coaching context relies on WebSearch.

  **WebSearch consensus**: NFC odds show LA clear favorite (+300 ≈25% implied), SEA next (+600 ≈14%), PHI/DET chase pack (+900/+930 ≈10%), SF/GB (+1000 ≈9%), DAL (+1200), CHI (+1400), MIN/TB (+2200). Separately confirmed (multi-source) the A.J. Brown trade details and Myles Garrett trade. A single-source Ringer article claims Bears and Commanders "will be without marquee starters for all of 2026" (unnamed players — treated as an unconfirmed directional signal only) and separately corroborates (independently of the transaction data) that Branch/Joseph (DET) and Parsons (GB) are sidelined to start the season — this second claim I treat as confirmed since it lines up with the structured transaction data. No coaching change was found for PHI in any source (reasonable inference of continuity, not confirmed).

  Baseline probabilities were built as a blend of the retrieved EPA/defense metrics, the confirmed transactions above, and the WebSearch consensus odds, normalized to sum to 100. For the scenario, reversing the A.J. Brown trade restores PHI's top perimeter WR (paired with DeVonta Smith), materially strengthening an offense that was otherwise thinner at the position this season; I moved PHI from the "chase pack" toward a share close to DET/GB, funding the increase proportionally from all 15 other teams.

